# CLAUDE.md

Selenium automation example in python

Uses `uv` for environment/dependency management and `just` as the command runner.

## Commands

- `just setup` - install Homebrew tools (`Brewfile`) and sync the project
- `just sync` - install all dependency groups into `.venv`
- `just lint` - type check (ty), lint + autofix (ruff), format (ruff), spell check (codespell),
  workflow lint (actionlint)
- `just ci-lint` - same checks without modifying files (used to verify, not fix)
- `just test` - run pytest with coverage (fails under 98%)
- `just audit` - check dependencies for known vulnerabilities (pip-audit)
- `just markdownlint` - lint Markdown files (markdownlint-cli2, config in `.markdownlint-cli2.jsonc`)
- `just docs-build` - build the docs with Zensical in strict mode (`zensical.toml`, pages in `docs/`)
- `just docs-serve` - serve the docs locally with live reload
- `just zizmor` - audit GitHub Actions workflows for security issues
- `just git-leaks` - scan staged changes for secrets
- `uv add <pkg>` / `uv add --dev <pkg>` - add a runtime / dev dependency (never edit `uv.lock` by hand)
- `uv run python-selenium` - run the app entry point

Run `just lint` and `just test` before considering a change done.

## Layout

- `src/python_selenium/` - the package (src layout, built with `uv_build`, installed editable by `uv sync`)
- `src/python_selenium/__init__.py` - `main()` entry point, exposed as the `python-selenium` script
- `tests/` - pytest tests; import the package as `from python_selenium.<module> import ...`
- `prek.toml` - git hook config (`prek install` to enable)
- `.github/workflows/` - `python.yml` (lint, tests, docs build, markdownlint),
  `security.yml` (zizmor, gitleaks, pip-audit)
- `.github/dependabot.yml` - weekly updates for actions, uv, dev container image and features
- `.devcontainer/` - dev container; base image, `just`, and `uv` pinned by tag + digest
- `scripts/` - repo maintenance scripts

## Conventions

- Python >= 3.14; ruff line length 100, double quotes
- Docstrings required in `src/` (ruff `D` rules), not in `tests/`
- Type hints on public functions; code must pass `ty check`
- Renaming the project means updating `[project] name`, the `src/<name>/` folder, and `[project.scripts]` together

## CI and security

- Pin GitHub Actions to a full commit SHA with a version comment (`uses: owner/action@<sha> # vX.Y.Z`);
  run `just zizmor` after editing workflows
- Give each workflow/job least-privilege `permissions`; set `persist-credentials: false` on checkout
  unless the job pushes
- Pin Docker images as `image:tag@sha256:<digest>`
- uv is pinned to 0.13.x in four places that must stay in sync: `[tool.uv] required-version` and the
  `uv_build` requirement in `pyproject.toml`, `setup-uv` `version` in the workflows, and the uv image in
  `.devcontainer/Dockerfile`
